# Overnight Execution Plan for One M1 Pro and CPU Box

- Phase 1 (Hours 0 - 2, CPU): Implement Proposal 3 (Color Gating) and Proposal 1 (Region Partition & Aggregation). Test both directly on cached probability maps (`DOMAIN_CACHE` and `HGB_CACHE`) using `research_v5/devharness.py`. This requires zero neural training and delivers immediate diagnostic numbers on the development split.
- Phase 2 (Hours 2 - 4, CPU): Implement Proposal 2 (Unsupervised Prototype Competition) on stride-8 texture features. Evaluate fusion between competitive probabilities and region boundary aggregation.
- Phase 3 (Hours 4 - 10, Apple M1 Pro MPS): Launch overnight fine-tuning of HatchFinder with Lovasz loss and in-drawing hard negative mining (`train_hatchfinder.py` modified for document hard negative sampling). Let it train for 800 steps on fit split overnight.
- Phase 4 (Morning evaluation): Run the overnight-trained HatchFinder through the Phase 1/2 region-aggregation and color-gating pipeline using `devharness.py` to obtain the final development-selected score.
